# Copyrighted material. Nothing in this list may ever be committed.
#
# The disc images and ROMs are commercial, still-in-copyright software. They are
# not distributed with this repository. Anyone who wants them gets them from
# archive.org themselves, per README.md section 0. Only scripts, tests and
# documentation belong in git.
#
# Adding a rule here is cheap. Committing a game file is not recoverable, because
# history is forever and a rewrite does not un-distribute it. When in doubt,
# ignore.

# --- Game data -------------------------------------------------------------

# Disc images. CloneCD trio, ISO, Alcohol, raw bin/cue.
*.img
*.sub
*.cue
*.ccd
*.iso
*.mds
*.mdf
*.bin
*.nrg
*.toast
*.dmg

# Floppy and hard disk images (the FM Towns save floppy lives here).
*.hdm
*.HDM
*.d77
*.d88
*.hdf
*.vhd
*.fdi
*.2hd

# Archive formats. A .zip of the retail release is the single most likely way
# for copyrighted data to arrive by accident.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.lzh
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Executables and libraries from the disc, even if extracted somewhere tidy.
*.exe
*.EXE
*.exp
*.EXP
*.Exp
*.com
*.COM
*.sys
*.SYS
*.drv
*.DRV
*.386
*.rex
*.REX

# Any surviving dump of the game files themselves. Both cases are listed
# because gitignore patterns are case-sensitive and FM Towns and DOS tooling
# upper-cases extensions. *.TIF in particular will slip through a *.tif rule.
*.snd
*.SND
*.eup
*.EUP
*.fmb
*.FMB
*.tif
*.TIF
*.tiff
*.TIFF
*.mp3
*.MP3
*.mp2
*.MP2
*.mp1
*.MP1
*.dg3
*.DG3
*.dic
*.DIC
*.fnt
*.FNT

# --- Case-insensitive safety net ------------------------------------------
# Enumerating every mixed-case spelling is a losing game, as z.Eup proved.
# These patterns catch any capitalisation of the extensions that matter.
*.[eE][xX][pP]
*.[eE][xX][eE]
*.[cC][oO][mM]
*.[sS][yY][sS]
*.[tT][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
*.[sS][nN][dD]
*.[eE][uU][pP]
*.[fF][mM][bB]
*.[mM][pP][0-9]
*.[dD][gG][0-9]
*.[hH][dD][mM]
*.[dD]77
*.[zZ][iI][pP]
*.[rR][aA][rR]
*.[lL][zZ][hH]
*.[dD][iI][cC]
*.[fF][nN][tT]

# --- Vendored third-party binaries -----------------------------------------
# tools/vendor.sh downloads Tsugaru and the FreeTowns ROMs here. Third-party
# binaries, gitignored as a unit.
/vendor/

# --- Emulator and ROMs -----------------------------------------------------

# Tsugaru binaries and ROM sets are downloaded per README, never committed.
# ROMs are copyrighted whether dumped from hardware or not.
/emulator/
*.rom
*.ROM
*.DAT
*.dat

# Extracted artwork and audio formats. A stray .png or .wav in the repo root is
# just as much derived copyrighted content as the original disc file.
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[bB][mM][pP]
*.[wW][aA][vV]
*.[fF][lL][aA][cC]

# --- Derived output --------------------------------------------------------

# Extracted artwork and audio is derived from copyrighted data. Same rule.
/extracted/
/analysis/
/output/
/build/

# --- Runtime state ---------------------------------------------------------

/saves/
CMOS.BIN
*.log
*.tmp

# MkDocs build output. Built in CI and assembled with web/ into the Pages
# artefact, so it never needs to be in git.
/_site/
/site/

# --- Tooling noise ---------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
package-lock.json
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- Third-party reference clones ------------------------------------------
# Other people's reimplementations, cloned for cross-checking formats. They are
# not ours, they are large, and they carry their own licences. Never committed.
references/

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A GitHub token lives in .env for pushing. It must never be committed, and the
# case-insensitive block covers .ENV and .Env, which a case-sensitive rule
# would miss on this machine.
.env
*.env
*.ENV
*.Env
!.env.example
__pycache__/
